```dart
/// Collapses one blank run in [lines]: the run containing or adjacent to
/// [index] (a kept-coordinate index; may be out of range = no-op).
/// [dropEntirely] removes the run instead of keeping one blank (used
/// when the vacated span sat at the answer's edge).
```

Cases:
- Right seam: run starting at kept index `span.startLine` (if < kept.length and blank).
- Left seam: run ending at kept index `span.startLine - 1` (if >= 0 and blank).

Edge cases:
- Span at text start (span.startLine == 0): left seam doesn't exist; right run at index 0 is a LEADING blank run → drop entirely.
- Span at text end (span.endLine == lines.length - 1): the right seam index == kept.length (out of range) → no right run. Left run at kept index span.startLine - 1 == kept.length - 1 is a TRAILING run → drop entirely.

Implementation:

```dart
String _stripSpan(String text, _LedgerSpan span) {
  final lines = text.split('\n');
  final kept = <String>[
    for (var i = 0; i < lines.length; i++)
      if (i < span.startLine || i > span.endLine) lines[i],
  ];
  // Right seam: the first line after the vacated range, at kept index
  // span.startLine. A blank run there is leading when the span started
  // the answer (index 0) — the edge the ledger vacated drops entirely.
  _collapseSeamBlank(kept, span.startLine, span.startLine == 0);
  // Left seam: the last line before the vacated range. A blank run there
  // is trailing when the span ended the answer.
  _collapseSeamBlank(kept, span.startLine - 1, span.endLine == lines.length - 1);
  return kept.join('\n');
}

/// Collapses the maximal blank run touching kept-coordinate [index] to a
/// single blank line — or removes it entirely when [dropEntirely] (the
/// run is the answer's leading/trailing edge left blank by the removal).
/// Out-of-range and non-blank indices are no-ops.
void _collapseSeamBlank(List<String> lines, int index, bool dropEntirely) {
  if (index < 0 || index >= lines.length) return;
  if (lines[index].trim().isNotEmpty) return;
  var start = index;
  while (start > 0 && lines[start - 1].trim().isEmpty) {
    start--;
  }
  var end = index;
  while (end + 1 < lines.length && lines[end + 1].trim().isEmpty) {
    end++;
  }
  final replacement = dropEntirely ? const <String>[] : const [''];
  lines.replaceRange(start, end + 1, replacement);
}
```

